fact("ledger-deaf-p3-fix") = {
  body:  "LEDGER-DEAF-P3 fixed by consolidating S3* to ONE shared NATS connection. Root cause: S3* held TWO NATS connections — the ingest connection (subscription=1, writer driven by event loop) worked, but the emit connection (publish-only, subscriptions=0) had a dead async-nats writer. publish() and flush() returned Ok(()) but nothing reached the wire (in_msgs=0 on broker CID for 5+ days). Claude [O] wrote the fix in commit 1396c7b: removed emit::maybe_connect_nats() and passed nats.clone() to ingest::start_ingest_task so BOTH ingest subscribe and emit publish share ONE connection whose subscription keeps the async-nats writer alive.",
  why:   "This closes P0 LEDGER-DEAF-P3. The algedonic channel from S3* to the ledger was completely broken since Jul 11 — 164 findings queued in events.jsonl but never published to NATS.",
  apply: "Do NOT create separate NATS clients for subscribe vs publish in async-nats 0.49. Every client that needs to publish must carry at least one subscription to keep its writer event loop driven.",
}

